  "id": "intention-movement",
  "term": "intention movement",
  "definition": "Intention movement refers to the brain state in which a person intends to make a movement before the movement is carried out. In this state, activity and connectivity in motor-related brain networks differ from resting and execution states, allowing the upcoming movement to be predicted.",
